//! The `text-box` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property corresponds to the `text-box-trim` and `text-box-edge` properties, which together
//! specify the amount of space to trim from the block-start edge and block-end edge of a text
//! element's block container.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The default value. Equivalent to the `text-edge` value `text`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-edge
//! - none: The default value. No space is trimmed from the text. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim
//! - text: The font's over edge is its text-over baseline (includes the font's ascenders but
//! excludes the over edge half-leading), or its under edge is its text-under baseline (includes the
//! font's descenders but excludes the under edge half-leading), depending on which edge the value is
//! set for. See https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/text-edge
//! - trim-both: The start (over) and end (under) edges are both trimmed. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim
//! - trim-end: The end (under) edge is trimmed. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim
//! - trim-start: The start (over) edge is trimmed. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box-trim
//!
//! Grammar: normal | <'text-box-trim'> || <'text-box-edge'>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline-3/#propdef-text-box
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/text-box
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

